"ux_account_help" = "Account access\nYour private key works like a password. Keep it secret and store it outside this phone. It cannot be reset.\n\nYour data\nA key copy is not a data backup. Your logbook and lists need a separate backup.\n\nOptional tools\nAmber can manage your key in a separate app. Your public account ID can be shared, but cannot restore access.";
"ux_grade_progression_help" = "Four-week window\nEach point uses up to three hardest distinct climb-and-angle combinations sent within that week and the previous three weeks, within the selected period. Repeats at the same angle count once.\n\nLevel\nWith three results, the middle grade is used; with two, their average; with one, its grade. Only successful entries with a known grade contribute.";
"ux_later_send" = "Later send";
"ux_lists_help" = "Lists\nA list contains each climb once. Favourites are a built-in list.\n\nPlayback\nAn optional plan adds repeated climbs, angles and rests. Playing it does not automatically mean you climbed its steps. Record attempts and sends in the logbook.\n\nHistory\nHistory records climbs sent to the board LEDs. It is separate from your climbing logbook.";
"ux_logbook_help" = "Entries\nSends are successful log entries, including repeats. Attempts here are entries without a send. An entry can include several tries.\n\nFilters\nOutcome, board and angle narrow this list. The period selected in statistics also applies to this list; the statistics board filter is separate. Lighting a climb on the board does not log a climbing attempt.";
"ux_logbook_unsent_attempts" = "Without a send";
"ux_outcome_donut_hint" = "Each sent climb counts once per board family in this period, across angles: Flash or a later send. Unsuccessful climbs are not part of this ring.";
"ux_plan_title" = "Playback plan";
"ux_profile_identity" = "Name and pictures";
"ux_profile_links" = "Links and addresses (optional)";
"ux_restore_consequence" = "Restoring uses the previous account and enables encrypted backup. You will confirm the account change before continuing.";
"ux_sent_climbs" = "Sent climbs";
"ux_sent_climbs_grade" = "Sent climbs and repeats by grade";
"ux_stats_help" = "Volume\nSends count successful entries, including repeats. Attempts add up the recorded tries in all entries, including sends; each entry counts at least once.\n\nProblem outcomes\nEach climb counts once per board family in the selected period, across angles: Flash, otherwise Sent, otherwise Attempted. For a flash, the first recorded entry for that climb at that angle must be a send with at most one try. Earlier attempts rule it out, even outside the selected period. Missing history limits this classification. The flash rate divides flashes by successful entries, including repeats.\n\nActivity and time chart\nThese count log entries, including unsuccessful entries, rather than individual tries or only sends. Records use the full history; other charts follow the selected period.";
